{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Ringed.</b> On the leg, and the meaning is a marking that rings the leg." "<b>And speckled.</b> That which has speckles." "<b>And streaked.</b> From the derivation of ברד, that which has white markings." "And the word טלוא is a general term, and it is derived from \"בלות ומטולאית\" (Joshua 9:5), and the meaning is like שומית, and the sense of כל שה נקוד וטליא is every speckled sheep and kid, and likewise it is written \"שה כשבים ושה עזים\" (Deuteronomy 14:4). And since טלוא is a general term, behold, it explained: every speckled and ringed and streaked male goat." "<b>And every dark sheep.</b> These are the dark ones, and it is possible that the dark ones are so called because of חום, for the dark ones are more חום than white." "<b>And streaked and speckled among the goats.</b> Ringed and streaked and speckled."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:28.416113587Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}